#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0538 expect=violation domain=DS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a subject has more than one Disposition Event record (DSCAT equals 'DISPOSITION EVENT') per Epoch (EPOCH) and more than one of those records has Subcategory for Disposition Event (DSSCAT) equal to 'STUDY PARTICIPATION'.
#note "EPOCH ABSENT -- the D17 pin. Byte-for-byte the CDISC-CG0538-invalid-DS-1 violating rows with the Permissible EPOCH column removed and nothing else changed. This file previously asserted expect=noViolation: the rule carried an authored 'name: EPOCH / operator: exists' leaf, which is false on an absent column and killed the whole all:. D17 removed that guard -- it has no basis in either sheet column (neither the Condition 'Subject has more than one record per Epoch with DSCAT = DISPOSITION EVENT' nor the Rule 'No more than 1 record per subject has DSSCAT = STUDY PARTICIPATION' asks for EPOCH to be collected) -- so the rule now agrees with its own sheet, and with its CORE twin CORE-000214-invalid_no_epoch-DS-1.cdt, which carries byte-identical rows and has always expected a violation. Every remaining leaf holds: the gate record_count(DSCAT, filter=DSCAT='DISPOSITION EVENT', group=[USUBJID, EPOCH]) ignores the absent EPOCH key and counts 2 per subject, so '> 1' holds; var_exists(DSSCAT) holds; DSSCAT equals the literal STUDY PARTICIPATION; and the uniqueness tuple repeats across both rows, so both are flagged. NOT vacuous, and it isolates D17 rather than D16: with EPOCH absent, is_not_unique_set already dropped the absent key and regrouped on (DSSCAT, USUBJID) before D16 removed EPOCH from the declared list, so D16 is a no-op on these rows and the guard is the whole difference. This file is RED against the guarded rule. It was renamed from CDISC-CG0538-valid_no_epoch-DS-1.cdt, whose name no longer described what it asserts."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 DSSEQ=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
#expectViolationAt row=2 DSSEQ=2 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT   type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col DSSCAT  type=Char label="Subcategory for Disposition Event"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION
---
